{"content":[{"c":["SHALMAN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Unknown conqueror whose brutal destruction of Beth-arbel was descriptive of Israel’s approaching judgment (",{"href":"?bref=Hos.10.14","r":"Hos.10.14","rawR":"Hos.10.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hos.10.14","value":"Hos.10.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hos 10:14"},"). Several suggestions as to the identification of Shalman are the following: Salamanu, the king of Moab who paid tribute to Tiglath-pileser of Assyria; one of the Shalmaneser kings of Assyria; and Shalmah, a north Arabian tribe that invaded the Negev."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Shalman","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Hos 10:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Hos.10.14","rawQueryValue":"Hos.10.14","sourceRefExact":"Hos.10.14"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"a06ad84de6f109f81392611f1e2a37aae22dbb3ed78b6be7753c9d7ba4364710","sourceItemName":"Shalman","sourceItemOrder":193,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Shalman","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Shalman","title":"Shalman","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}